digraph decision {
  rankdir=TB;
  bgcolor="#0d0e12";
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, fillcolor="#181a20", color="#343846", fontcolor="#e2e8f0"];
  edge [color="#64748b", fontcolor="#94a3b8", fontsize=9, fontname="Helvetica"];

  // 1. Prior-journal learning pass
  history [
    label="1. Prior-journal learning pass (python3 scripts/stats.py, 2026-10-25T12:19Z)\nSettled before this run: EXPIRED+1.14% ZECUSDT (SHORT), EXPIRED+3.95% ASTERUSDT (LONG), EXPIRED AVAXUSDT (never filled),\nLOSS-1.08% ETHUSDT, LOSS-1.30% XRPUSDT, LOSS-1.01% ASTERUSDT, LOSS-1.50% ZECUSDT. Arithmetic sum +0.20%; win rate 0/4 in WIN/LOSS terms;\navg loss -1.22%. PENDING XRPUSDT (expires 2026-10-26T21:00Z) and the IDEA of this run untouched.\n\nLessons with evidence, checked against each review.md + trade.toml + outcome_candles.csv:\n* LOSS-1.08%_2026-10-18T1703Z_ETHUSDT, LOSS-1.50%_2026-10-23T1147Z_ZECUSDT and LOSS-1.01%_2026-10-23T1024Z_ASTERUSDT were all\n  stopped 1.0-1.5% from entry while the intended direction later resumed (ASTER 0.695 entry / 0.688 stop was stopped on 2026-10-24T14:15Z\n  and the pair traded 0.7041 by 2026-10-25T09:55Z, i.e. the original 0.706 target became reachable after the stop). Stops measured in\n  a fixed 1-1.5% are inside ordinary noise. APPLIED HERE: this is a 5.14%-ATR daily chart, so the structurally motivated stop sits 1.27 ATR\n  from entry (2.34) and the tighter 2.285 alternative was rejected as noise-prone (Jev: 0.61 that 2.19/2.285 gets noise-stopped).\n* LOSS-1.30%_2026-10-19T1533Z_XRPUSDT (same failure mode, same symbol family): stop just above a supply band inside a squeeze. APPLIED:\n  stop placed beyond the measured Oct 21 high 2.2652 and beyond the 38.2% retrace 2.3348 instead of hugging the supply shelf.\n* EXPIRED_2026-10-18T1730Z_AVAXUSDT: a LIMIT that never filled expired unused and cost nothing. APPLIED: fill probability is asked of Jev\n  separately and priced separately from the outcome conditional on a fill; an unfilled order is never counted as a win or a loss.\n* EXPIRED+1.14%_2026-10-19T1143Z_ZECUSDT: filled, missed target, expired +1.14%. APPLIED: non-target outcomes are not all full losses, so the\n  order-level number is reported alongside the TP/SL conditional rather than folding expiry into the stop bucket.\nSample is 7 settled trades; no aggregate win-rate or directional inference is drawn from it.",
    fillcolor="#1e293b", color="#3b82f6"
  ];

  // 2. Chart extraction
  extract [
    label="2. Extraction and measurement (from the image, then cross-checked)\nFrame: 261025_13h18m38s_screenshot.png = CAKEUSDT 1D Aster, clock 13:18:37 UTC+1 -> 2026-10-25T12:18Z.\nHeader: O2.0800 H2.0928 L2.0455 C2.0715 (-0.37 / -0.18%).\nPipeline (stdlib PNG inflate, no OCR): candle colour mask green(30,124,87)/red(173,69,70) -> vertical-run filter >=2 px ->\n797 bar columns merged into 197 daily bars. Price axis: 21 horizontal gridlines at y=73..993, exactly 46 px apart -> linear scale\nprice = 3.0 - (y-73)/460, i.e. 0.10 per 46 px. Time axis: vertical month gridlines x=205(May 1),438(Jun 1),663,896,1129,1355(Oct 1),\n1588,1814 -> 7.5187 px/day; bars run x=62..1535 = 2026-04-12..2026-10-25 (198 days).\nVALIDATION: frame tags 2.8606 (y137), 2.0715 (y500) and 1.1271 (y934) reproduce within 1.5 px; last bar O2.0804 H2.0935 L2.0478 C2.0739\nvs header O2.0800 H2.0928 L2.0455 C2.0715 (<=1.5 px); Oct 19-25 bars vs Binance 1d klines within 0.35% on every field except the\n2026-10-23 low (extracted 2.0739 vs Binance 2.104 - a 1.4% wick difference attributed to venue, Aster vs Binance).\nArtifacts corrected during extraction: the legend text at y51-60 and the dotted last-price row y=500 were excluded.\n\nMeasured structure:\n* 2026-04-12 ~1.50 -> May cap 1.6457 -> June 5 low 1.1304 (frame tag 1.1271) -> June-July base 1.30-1.48.\n* Mid-Aug breakout (week of Aug 17: 1.4522 -> 1.8565) -> parabolic advance 1.3891 -> 2.8587 on 2026-09-27 (+106% in ~7 weeks).\n* Reversal: week of Sep 28 high 2.8370 close 2.5087; then three consecutive lower weekly highs AND closes:\n  2.5565/2.3652, 2.4326/2.1848, 2.2652/2.0739.\n* Decline 2.8587 -> 2.0109 (2026-10-24 low) = -29.66% over 27 days.\n* Lower highs: 2.8587 / 2.5565 / 2.4326 / 2.2848 / 2.2652 / 2.1935 / 2.1326. Lows: 2.0826 (Oct 8) / 2.1087 (Oct 18) / 2.1130 (Oct 22) /\n  2.0739 (Oct 23) / 2.0109 (Oct 24). Oct 24 candle O2.1196 H2.1326 L2.0109 C2.0761 - long lower tail, closed near the low of its range.\n* SMA5 2.1291, SMA10 2.1606, SMA20 2.2109, SMA50 2.3552, SMA100 1.9574. ATR14 0.1065 (5.14% of price), ATR7 4.03%,\n  daily close-to-close stdev 2.11%, RSI14 22.5. Close 2.8% below SMA20 and 12% below SMA50.\n* Fib of the rally 1.3891->2.8587: 23.6% 2.5119, 38.2% 2.2973, 50% 2.1239, 61.8% 1.9505. Fib of the decline 2.8587->2.0109:\n  23.6% 2.2110, 38.2% 2.3348, 50% 2.4348.\n* No volume pane in the frame: volume is not measurable and was not used.\n* Live re-anchor 2026-10-25T12:46:18Z: spot 2.0640, perp mark 2.0608, day range 2.0460-2.0990, rolling 24h -1.81%.",
    fillcolor="#0f2a43", color="#38bdf8"
  ];

  // 3. Scenarios
  scenarios [
    label="3. Scenarios built from the measured chart (not a fixed menu)\nS1 bounce-then-roll (forecast): price holds the 2.01-2.08 shelf, grinds up into 2.13-2.19 (falling SMA20 2.2109 / Oct 19-23 supply /\n   23.6% retrace 2.2110), fails there and rolls over through 2.01 toward the 1.95-1.96 confluence (61.8% retrace 1.9505 + SMA100 1.9574).\nS2 immediate continuation: 2.0109 breaks within a day or two and the decline extends to 1.9152 / 1.8565 without a bounce.\nS3 range: 2.00-2.26 chop for the whole window; neither edge is decisively broken.\nS4 genuine reclaim: 2.2652 is reclaimed and the lower-high sequence ends, opening 2.3348 / 2.4326.\nS5 deep flush: 1.95 gives way quickly toward 1.78-1.86 (top of the August base).\nJev on the set as a whole: 'stays inside 2.00-2.26 for most of the window' 0.50; 'unfinished distribution, further downside to 1.85-1.95\nlikelier than recovery above 2.43' 0.67; 'deep retrace to 1.95 likelier than a shallow end near 2.08' 0.56; 'new low below 2.0109\ninside the window' 0.50; 'next 3-5 days is an orderly bounce into 2.13-2.21 rather than immediate continuation below 2.00' 0.53.\nThe scenarios are not treated as a mutually exclusive probability set; each Jev number below is recorded as the separate proposition asked.",
    fillcolor="#1e1b4b", color="#8b5cf6"
  ];

  // 4. Jev battery 1 - chart only
  jev1 [
    label="4. Jev, chart-only state (jev_noul, 2026-10-25T12:32Z). Propositions and probabilities as asked:\n* 'trades at or below 1.95 before at or above 2.26, 2026-10-25T12:30Z..2026-11-04T12:30Z' = 0.43\n* mirror 'at or above 2.26 before at or below 1.95' = 0.50  (the two do not sum to 1: 7% neither edge)\n* '2.01-2.08 shelf is genuine demand whose next test produces a >=4% bounce before a decisive break' = 0.48\n* 'decline is an unfinished distribution; further downside to 1.85-1.95 likelier than full recovery above 2.43 in two weeks' = 0.67\n* 'a >=+5% bounce from 2.07 within 5 days before any break below 2.00' = 0.45\n* 'parabolic shape makes a deep retrace to 1.95 likelier than a shallow one ending near 2.08' = 0.56\n* 'stays inside 2.00-2.26 for most of the window' = 0.50\n* 'RSI14 22.5 plus the Oct 24 lower tail means exhausted selling rather than a pause before another leg down' = 0.38\n* 'external information could materially change the 10-day direction forecast' = 0.94 (auto)\n* 'a focused research pass would materially change the trade taken today' = 0.82\nReading: the immediate barrier race is close to even with a slight upside tilt, while the deeper structural read is bearish.\nMarkets entries on BOTH sides fail on that basis (see 8), which is why the work moved to limit entries at measured levels.",
    fillcolor="#14261c", color="#22c55e"
  ];

  // 5. Research
  research [
    label="5. Research (agenda set by Jev; two passes; dated findings in research_log.txt)\njev_decide on the agenda: dated catalyst calendar 0.59 / positioning 0.34 / spot flows 0.02 / beta-sector 0.02.\nAn earlier Jev answer put 0.82 on 'the unresolved closing date of the PancakeSwap vote could change the decision', which is why a second,\ntargeted pass was run instead of stopping after round 1.\nRound 1 (2026-10-25T12:31-12:50Z): no bearish CAKE-specific dated catalyst inside the window. In-window macro: FOMC 2026-10-28T18:00Z,\nQ3 GDP + Sept PCE 2026-10-29T12:30Z, ECI 10-30, JOLTS 11-02, NFP 2026-11-06T13:30Z; October CPI 11-10 and PPI 11-13 fall outside.\nFunding -0.000689%/8h (flat), OI ~4.37M CAKE (~$9M, small): no crowding. CAKE -27.2% since Sep 27 vs BTC -5.0%: idiosyncratic.\nRound 2 (2026-10-25T12:38-12:55Z): 'The Flip' vote CLOSED 2026-10-24T08:07:22Z - before the window - read in full from the Snapshot\nHub GraphQL proposal object in cakevote.eth. It passed 70.9/29.1 but one address supplied 3,010,422.78 of the 3,037,343.96 For votes\n(99.1%); a 2026-10-23T17:16:38Z forum post alleges that address is an old treasury wallet (unverified, unrefuted). Content: 88/12 LP fee\nsplit, emissions 22,500 -> 7,000 CAKE/day routed to a growth fund rather than burned, 12% protocol fee to Treasury; the team concedes\n'weekly net burn would be lower' and calls lower Treasury income 'a deliberate short-term sacrifice'. Activation 'begins in November 2026,\nwithin 2 weeks of passing', no date -> on or before about 2026-11-07. The -4.83% day was 2026-10-22, before the decisive vote, so the drop\ncannot be pinned on the outcome. Gaps recorded: no readable full text of the Oct 21 news item, degraded news search (so 'no hack/delisting'\nis not a clean negative), no Aster funding/OI, no blog-posted activation date.\nJev on the findings: 'contradicts the bearish continuation read' 0.14 then 0.12 (auto) - research did NOT overturn the chart; 'the\ngovernance allegation, if it gains traction, pushes CAKE toward 1.95 rather than 2.26' 0.78; 'emissions cut + weaker burn is a mild net\nnegative over two weeks' 0.70; 'findings change side/entry/stop/target' 0.59; 'another research pass is still needed' 0.33 -> research stopped.",
    fillcolor="#14261c", color="#22c55e"
  ];

  // 6. Jev battery 2 - levels, conditionals, stop survivability
  jev2 [
    label="6. Jev, level and conditional battery (jev_noul). Each row is the exact proposition asked and its probability.\n* touch >=2.15 before <=1.96 = 0.42 | touch >=2.19 before <=1.96 = 0.41 | touch <=1.945 before >=2.19 = 0.37\n* touch >=2.19 at ANY point by 2026-11-08 = 0.58 | by 2026-11-04 = 0.62 | by 2026-10-31 = 0.51\n* touch >=2.21 at ANY point in the window = 0.46 | touch >=2.15 at any point = 0.66 | touch <=1.96 at any point = 0.66\n* if touch <=2.02 then >=2.13 before <=1.945 = 0.33   -> a long off this shelf with a nearby target is NOT supported\n* if touch <=1.96 then >=2.14 before <=1.90 = 0.41 | 'the 1.90 stop is noise-hit before 2.14 is reached' = 0.60 -> long candidate rejected\n* if touch >=2.15 then <=1.96 before >=2.285 = 0.44 | if touch >=2.19 then <=1.96 before >=2.285 = 0.39\n* if touch >=2.21 then <=1.96 before >=2.34 = 0.67 | mirror '>=2.34 before <=1.96' = 0.20 | '<=2.0109 before >=2.34' = 0.63\n* 'a 2.19 entry with a 2.285 stop would be taken out by ordinary noise' = 0.61 | 'a 2.34 stop on a 2.21 entry survives a normal bounce' = 0.69\n* '2.19-2.21 would be a selling opportunity in a continuing decline' = 0.73 | 'next 5 days touch 2.19 before 1.96' = 0.57\n* 'a short near 2.19-2.21 targeting 1.96 is better supported than a long at 1.96 targeting 2.14' = 0.74\n* 'a short 2.21 / 1.96 / 2.34 is a coherent expression of this chart' = 0.85 (auto)\n* 'the shelf is defended in the next 5 days' = 0.41 | 'FOMC 2026-10-28 warrants a shorter expiry' = 0.31 | '14-day expiry fits better than ~2026-11-01' = 0.41\n* 'extending past the 2026-11-10 CPI would materially improve the outcome' = 0.18 | 'a fill on/after 2026-11-03 is unlikely to reach 1.96 by 11-08' = 0.34\nCONFLICTS NOTICED AND HANDLED: the conditional '<=1.96 before >=2.34' (0.67) is inconsistent with the nearer '<=2.0109 before >=2.34' (0.63),\nand 'touch >=2.19 by 11-04' (0.62) is inconsistent with 'by 11-08' (0.58). Treated as estimator noise, not as independent votes: the\nfinal post-fill win probability used for the arithmetic is 0.55, asked for the exact ticket in 9, and the EV was stress-tested from 0.35 to 0.70.",
    fillcolor="#272015", color="#eab308"
  ];

  // 7. Candidate construction
  candidates [
    label="7. Candidates (LONG and SHORT evaluated independently; levels taken from measured structure, no preset distances)\nEvery entry is a level price actually visited (2.19 = Oct 19/20/23 highs; 2.21 = SMA20 + 23.6% retrace; 1.96 = 61.8% retrace + SMA100;\n2.02 = top of the Oct 24 wick). Breakout entries are outside this journal's model and were not proposed.\n\nMARKET SHORT 2.063 -> TP 1.96 / SL 2.19: gross +4.99% / -6.16%, break-even 0.552, Jev P(1.96 before 2.19) ~0.37-0.41 -> NEGATIVE EV.\nMARKET LONG 2.063 -> TP 2.19 / SL 1.945: gross +6.16% / -5.72%, break-even 0.482, Jev P(2.19 before 1.945) 0.41 -> NEGATIVE EV.\nLIMIT LONG 2.02 -> TP 2.13 / SL 1.945: break-even 0.405 vs Jev conditional 0.33 -> NEGATIVE EV. Rejected.\nLIMIT LONG 1.96 -> TP 2.14 / SL 1.90: break-even 0.250 vs Jev conditional 0.41 (looks positive) BUT 'the 1.90 stop is noise-hit before 2.14' = 0.60\n   and 'a short near 2.19-2.21 is better supported than this long' = 0.74 -> rejected on stop survivability and on direction.\nSHORT LIMIT 2.15 -> TP 1.96 / SL 2.285: break-even 0.415, pwin 0.44 -> EV/fill +0.37%, margin +2.5pp. Thin.\nSHORT LIMIT 2.19 -> TP 2.00 / SL 2.34: break-even 0.441, but Jev put only 0.01 on this variant against the 1.96 target.\nSHORT LIMIT 2.21 -> TP 1.96 / SL 2.34: break-even 0.342, fill 0.46, pwin 0.67 -> EV/order ~+2.0%. Runner-up (jev_decide 0.26).\nSHORT LIMIT 2.19 -> TP 1.96 / SL 2.34: break-even 0.395, fill 0.58-0.62, pwin 0.55 -> selected (jev_decide 0.68, no_trade 0.04).\njev_decide over the four finalists (requirements: stop survives a 5.14%-ATR bounce / entry likely to be touched / target at measured structure)\nreturned 2.19-1.96-2.34 0.68, 2.21-1.96-2.34 0.26, 2.19-2.00-2.34 0.01, no_trade 0.04; no requirement was contradicted for the winner.",
    fillcolor="#272015", color="#eab308"
  ];

  // 8. Exact economics
  math [
    label="8. Selected-ticket arithmetic (computed by script, not by Jev; no fees, funding or slippage exist in this journal's model)\nSHORT LIMIT 2.19 | TP 1.96 | SL 2.34 | place 2026-10-25T12:28Z | expire 2026-11-04T12:30Z\nGain (2.19-1.96)/2.19 = +10.502%      Loss (2.34-2.19)/2.19 = -6.849%      RR 1.534\nBreak-even win probability for a filled trade = 6.849/(10.502+6.849) = 0.3948\nP(fill = price touches 2.19 before expiry) = 0.62 (asked for <=2026-11-04) / 0.58 (asked for <=2026-11-08); 0.58 used in the headline\nP(TP 1.96 before SL 2.34 | fill), asked for this exact ticket over the exact window = 0.55   [break-even 0.3948 -> margin +0.155]\nEV per fill = 0.55*10.502 - 0.45*6.849 = +2.694%      EV per placed order = 0.58*2.694 = +1.563%\nP(no fill) 0.42 with payoff 0 (an unfilled LIMIT costs nothing).\nSensitivity per fill: pwin 0.70 +4.67% | 0.55 +2.69% | 0.50 +1.83% | 0.45 +0.96% | 0.40 +0.09% | 0.3948 0.00% | 0.35 -0.78%.\nSo the order keeps a positive expectation for any post-fill win probability above the 0.3948 break-even, which brackets the whole Jev range\n(0.39-0.67) and is positive at the central 0.55 with a 15.5pp margin. The 42% no-fill mass is charged at zero, not as a loss, and the\nTP/SL split is not forced onto expiry outcomes: if neither level is touched the trade settles as EXPIRED+/-% at the last close.\nStop placement audit: 2.34 is 1.27 ATR above entry and beyond the measured Oct 21 high 2.2652 and the 38.2% retrace 2.3348; the tighter 2.285\nwas dropped because Jev put 0.61 on it being noise-stopped (the exact failure mode of ETHUSDT/ZECUSDT/ASTERUSDT in section 1).",
    fillcolor="#1f242d", color="#38bdf8"
  ];

  // 9. Freshness + final validation
  fresh [
    label="9. Freshness re-anchor and final validation (2026-10-25T12:46:18Z)\nLive spot 2.0640 (bid 2.0640/ask 2.0650); perp mark 2.0608; 2026-10-25 day range 2.0460-2.0990 with the low in the 09:00Z hour and price\n+0.88% off it; rolling 24h -1.81%. The frame was captured at 12:18Z with 2.0715, so price is 0.4% below the captured close and the measured\nstructure is unchanged: still below 2.19, still inside the 2.01-2.08 shelf, still below SMA10/SMA20.\nJev on the live price: 'the setup that supports a short limit at 2.19 with a 1.96 target and a 2.34 stop is still intact' = 0.93 (auto);\n'placing this order today is better than placing no order' = 0.91 (auto); mirror 'placing no order is better' = 0.07 (auto) -> consistent.\n'If CAKEUSDT first trades at or above 2.19 within 2026-10-25T12:46Z..2026-11-04T12:30Z, then it trades at or below 1.96 before at or above\n2.34' = 0.55 (the ticket's own conditional, used in section 8); the 2.00-target version of the same question = 0.57.\n'the 2026-11-04T12:30Z expiry cuts off the part of the decline where 1.96 would most likely be reached' = 0.32 -> no reason to extend.\nExpiry choice: jev_decide 2026-11-01 0.01 / 2026-11-04 0.97 / 2026-11-08 0.02.",
    fillcolor="#1e293b", color="#3b82f6"
  ];

  // 10. Forecast
  forecast [
    label="10. Forecast (independent of the trade; contested)\nMost supported path: hold of 2.01-2.08 -> grind up into 2.12-2.19 over ~4-5 sessions (FOMC 10-28 and GDP/PCE 10-29 supply the volatility)\n-> rejection at the falling SMA20 / Oct supply shelf -> roll over through 2.01 toward 1.96 and then 1.95 beyond the horizon.\nDrawn daily closes: 2026-10-26 2.050, 10-27 2.085, 10-28 2.120, 10-29 2.160, 10-30 2.190 (touch of the entry zone), 10-31 2.150,\n11-01 2.100, 11-02 2.045, 11-03 2.000, 11-04 1.975 - i.e. the drawn path ends ~1.3% short of the 1.96 target at the horizon.\nContest, stated honestly: (a) P(>=2.26 before <=1.95) 0.50 vs 0.43 means an upside resolution is just as live as S1; (b) the descending-highs\nregression through the post-peak swing highs projects only ~2.07-2.10 by 2026-10-30, so a touch of 2.19 requires a wick ABOVE that line - the\ntrade leans on the falling SMA20 (2.2109) rather than on the trendline; (c) P(immediate continuation below 2.00) is roughly 0.45-0.47, which would\nrender the bounce leg of the forecast wrong while still landing near the target. The forecast was not bent to fit the ticket: the drawn path\nstops short of the TP at the horizon.",
    fillcolor="#1e1b4b", color="#8b5cf6"
  ];

  // 11. Decision
  decision [
    label="11. DECISION: SHORT LIMIT 2.19 | TP 1.96 | SL 2.34 | expire 2026-11-04T12:30Z (PENDING)\nWhy go: a measured lower-high sequence, three lower weekly closes, price below SMA10/20/50 and a -29.7% break of a parabolic advance with a\ncontested supply-reducing governance outcome and a mild net-negative emissions change; every market entry on either side is negative EV, so the\nonly positive expressions are limit entries at measured supply, of which the 2.19 fade with a 1.27-ATR stop is the best supported (Jev 0.68 of\nfour finalists, coherence 0.85, setup intact 0.93, order better than no order 0.91 vs 0.07).\nReady to reject if: the fill never comes (no cost), or the 2.2652/2.34 area is reclaimed, which is the drawn invalidation and the deeper\nstructural read (P 0.12-0.14 that research already contradicts the bearish case; P 0.20-0.33 that 2.34 is reached before 1.96).\nResidual uncertainty carried: conditional probabilities from Jev are not internally consistent (0.63 vs 0.67 on nested targets; 0.58 vs 0.62 on\nthe same touch over nested windows); the trade survives that noise only because break-even is 0.395; the forecast is contested with a ~0.5\nprobability of an upside resolution first; the deep-flush scenario S5 to 1.78-1.86 would hit the target later than expiry.",
    fillcolor="#2a1215", color="#ef4444"
  ];

  history -> extract;
  extract -> scenarios;
  scenarios -> jev1;
  jev1 -> research;
  research -> jev2;
  jev2 -> candidates;
  candidates -> math;
  math -> fresh;
  fresh -> forecast;
  forecast -> decision;
}